### Output Format
Respond with XML inside a `<claim_inventory>` root element (no other text):

```xml
<claim_inventory count="{total_claims}" source_claim_count="{total_R1_input_claims}">
  <claim id="C1" corroboration_count="{n}" agreement="{consensus|majority|divided|minority}">
    <text>Single atomic claim — one position, one sentence</text>
    <expert_ids>expert_01, expert_03</expert_ids>
  </claim>
  <!-- repeat for ALL distinct claims -->
</claim_inventory>
```

### Emergence space (§6)
If you notice positions that don't fit neatly into atomic claims — tensions, implicit assumptions, or structural patterns across experts — surface them as claims with a `type="emergent"` attribute. These are valuable signal.

### Self-check before outputting
Count your claims. Count the R1 input claims. If your count is less than 60% of the input, re-read the expert responses — you are almost certainly compressing.
